svg: size an image that omits width and height (#6266)

Manga EPUBs wrap each JPEG in <svg width="100%" height="100%"> with no
viewBox, and the <image> has no width or height. The renderer skipped any
image with a non-positive size, so the page was a blank letter sheet.
A missing side is the raster's pixel size (one side missing keeps the
aspect). When the root svg itself has only a percentage size and no
viewBox, that pixel size becomes the page.
